{
	title: 'Commit cards: a commit a Bash call makes is a card beside its result',
	spec: 'When a Bash call (foreground or background) creates commits (detection: task hy, before the result is written), each commit becomes its own history record, an output record with a commit block, written right after the record carrying the tool results: hash, short hash, subject, amend flag, repository directory, files with lines added and removed (one git show --numstat per commit, only when commits exist) and lines. It therefore has its own number, shown as its id (e.g. #s399, task 9p letter s), never a sub-index of the result record, whose number the call card hides. No other record carries it, so replay, older pages and links show it as recorded. Older histories that stored commits inside the tool result keep showing them as n.1. The transcript draws it as its own card in terminal and web, kind commit with config key blockVerbosityCommit (default short), following short/long (task hyt): its title row is committed <short hash> <subject> (amended for an amend) in the commit color; below it come the files with +/- counts, then the lines, cut to the short rows when short. Clients watching the session therefore see each commit in the transcript; other clients keep the commit notice of task hy. Its lines are those commits.committed gives (task sg0), which the model already gets in the Bash result. Commits Hal did not observe in a Bash call get no card.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Stored as ToolResultBlock.commits (CommitBlock: paths root-relative, hook lines kept), so items come from transcript.resultItems: result, images, then commits, keyed n.1, n.2. Shown as output items with commit (letter s), kind commit, cardVerbosityCommit default short; header Committed/Amended. Color key commitCard (web class .commit-card): a plain .commit class would recolor commit notice cards. A background job ending after its early result gets no card: its report is a message, not a tool_result; the hook lines still reach the model there.',
		'Since s398.1 confused the user (the result record s398 never shows: its call card shows t395), tools still return ToolResultBlock.commits, but turns.ts takes them off with commits.take before writing the results and commits.cards writes each as an output record { commit } with its own n, broadcast as an output event. Output records are not provider input. transcript.resultItems still reads commits from old results.'
